<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Croatia (925-1102)</h1><p class="st-meta">925 CE – 1102 CE · capital Biograd na Moru</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Medieval Croatian kingdom of the Trpimirović dynasty, which reached from the Drava to the Adriatic before passing to the Hungarian crown.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 925 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomislav-of-croatia">Tomislav</a>, ruler of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-croatia">Duchy of Croatia</a>, also held the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-pannonian-croatia">Duchy of Pannonian Croatia</a> and was addressed as king in papal letters. He had defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-invasions-of-europe">Hungarian raids</a> and the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simeon-i-of-bulgaria">Simeon I of Bulgaria</a>, uniting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> in one kingdom.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kings ruled with a council of nobles and bans, from royal seats such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knin">Knin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biograd-na-moru">Biograd na Moru</a> and Nin. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petar-kresimir-iv">Petar Krešimir IV</a> (1058–1074) brought the Byzantine Dalmatian towns under his control, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-zvonimir">Demetrius Zvonimir</a> was crowned by a papal legate in 1076, tying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> to the Reformed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baska-tablet">Baška tablet</a> records Zvonimir's gift in Glagolitic script.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-zvonimir">Zvonimir</a> died without heirs, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-i-of-hungary">Ladislaus I of Hungary</a> claimed the throne. The last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petar-snacic">Petar Snačić</a>, fell at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gvozd-mountain">Gvozd</a> in 1097, and in 1102 Coloman was crowned king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, beginning the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-croatia-1102-1526">Kingdom of Croatia</a> (1102-1526) in union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 925 CE – 1102 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:78.11%;width:3.52%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>925 CE – 1102 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Biograd na Moru</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tomislav, Petar Krešimir IV, Demetrius Zvonimir</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Croatian; Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a href="/countries/bosnia-and-herzegovina">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Croatia, Croatian Kingdom, Trpimirović Croatia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1014&amp;focus=kingdom-of-croatia-925-1102" aria-label="Kingdom of Croatia (925-1102) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5050 622 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Croatia (925-1102) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5370 878L5388 829M5370 878L5363 868M5370 878L5388 874M5370 878L5419 902"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5388 829h0M5